title: '[NORTH-STAR/DEFERRED] finish harness adapter unification around shared contracts and conformance'
---
This north-star is partially shipped, so the original “N wholly bespoke drifting bridges” premise is too broad. I002/J1-J5 now provides the canonical v1 message schema and aggregate conformance gate. Shared generated skill fragments carry the B098/B099 safety invariant and B207 advisory trust guidance across supported clients. Runtime-generated `agent-help` also derives MCP-facing capability help from one registry.

The remaining goal is N thin shims binding shared contracts where host extension surfaces allow it:

1. Add a canonical machine-readable resolved identity/config surface (the proposed `c2c env --json`) with documented precedence.
2. Reduce tool-definition drift between MCP, pi, plugins, and CLI without pretending closed harnesses expose identical APIs.
3. Treat the shared safety fragment as canonical prompt policy and add conformance checks proving every generated/installed harness contains it.
4. Define a shared lifecycle/delivery contract across distinct hook, Monitor, app-server, plugin, and wake surfaces. Host-specific extension points remain thin shims, not falsely identical APIs.
5. Add a cross-client conformance self-check for install, identity, schema-v1 output, hook non-interference, delivery, generated-artifact freshness, and uninstall ownership.

This is adapter unification, not making closed harnesses natively c2c-aware. I002 is complete and no longer a dependency. Initial adapter convergence does not depend on I008; future identity/trust fields remain additive schema-v2 work. Keep deferred until current host integrations are stable, then split these residuals into independently deliverable tasks.
